extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 3: England printed 53-54 (cache p054-p055, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the cache and checked against renders of printed 53 and 54, where the powers, skill list and equipment sit. The entry starts at The Star Child heading on printed 53 and ends at Cybernetics & Bionics at the foot of printed 54. || CATEGORY: the page heading says The Star Child O.C.C. and the stat block The Star Child R.C.C.; stored as an R.C.C., as its stat block and as the Earth Child it shares an introduction, a mechanism and an experience column with (printed 50-51). A race, so no occ_group and men_of_arms false; it prints its own related and secondary skills, stored as printed. || XP: the column headed Dubugghs, Earth & Star Child (so spelled) on the Experience Tables, printed 152 (cache p153), read off a render. Every low bound is the previous high plus one. || POOLS: human-form hit points not printed; P.E. + 1D6 per level as for the book''s other classes. P.P.E. is P.E. x2 with no gain by level (power 10). I.S.P. is M.E. + 4D6, +1D6+1 per level. || LIGHT FORM: the 20 M.D.C. per level aura belongs to the light form only, so it is not mdc_base, which would make the human form a mega-damage being too; second_form carries S.D.C. and hit points only. The form and its powers are special abilities in prose, and the +5 vs magic illusions (power 6) stays prose because it is the light form''s. The flyer tag is power 12, flight with no spell, psionic power or equipment. || BONUSES: printed 53 heads the numbered powers with only applicable when transformed, but the list includes P.P.E. and life span, so power 11''s bonuses are read as the character''s and stored: +1D6 M.E., +2D6 Spd, +2 initiative, +1 dodge, +1 roll with impact, +2 vs horror factor. || PSIONICS: major; eight powers from the Sensitive or Healing categories, usable in either form. || SKILLS: each base is the catalog base plus the printed bonus. Read Sensory Equipment is the catalog Sensory Equipment; Math: Basic is Mathematics: Basic. English has no language row and rides Language: Other at the printed 65% (row ruling, 2026-11-12: no language skill rows); two languages of choice at +15% are a two-pick Language: Other group. Pilot any is read to include the Horsemanship category at +5%. Hand to Hand: Basic is granted and Expert costs one other skill: costs { expert: 1 }. || EQUIPMENT: rope and/or nylon cord stored as rope, spikes as iron spikes, pouches or sacks as one pouch, wood staff or walking stick as a walking stick. Not stored: weapons of choice (none named), light body armor (traditional, not issued)."
