# Star Child

## Lore

Also called the Shining One, or Child of Lugh, an ancient Celtic and Welsh god. The star child''s power is made as the earth child''s is, but its focus is the sun, the stars and light of every kind: with a thought the star child becomes a humanoid figure of bright light. Like the druids star children hold life, nature and freedom in high regard, but they are nomads and adventurers rather than teachers or healers, and take action against injustice to life or land.

## GM Notes

Children of the stars come from one human clan, the Lleumar of Orkney, Scotland, about 2000 strong; their young are raised among the clan and most master the transformation by age six. A child of an earth child and a star child has the power but must choose one path. The shooting star is dangerous and should be used with great caution. Most star children are drawn to laser weapons and magic items and wear light white, silver or tan body armor.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'star-child');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'star-child';

